& [Status]
  + [implementation] complete_against_exact_Slice8_phase_lock
  + [authority] consumed_and_closed

& [Server]
  + cantor_compiler_mcp is a separate workspace crate and cantor-compiler-mcp is a no-argument stdio binary
  + exactly one tool named validate_native_lifecycle is advertised
  + the server owns no lifecycle state and changes no existing MCP tool discovery

& [TransportProjection]
  + one strict request object is decoded as NativeLifecycleValidationRequest and delegated once to validate_native_lifecycle_request
  + structuredContent is the exact serialized NativeLifecycleValidationResponse returned by the core
  + is_error is false only for artifact_valid or verification_valid and true for lifecycle_refused or input_refused
  + response serialization failure is converted fail-closed into an input refusal

& [BoundsAndMetadata]
  + the complete MCP argument is measured before typed dispatch against the core eight-megabyte ceiling plus 65536 wrapper bytes
  + unknown missing extra and oversized arguments refuse before semantic replay
  + metadata is closed read-only nondestructive idempotent and closed-world
  + short text directs callers to structuredContent and preserves the distinction between coherence and authority

& [NoEffect]
  + no provider model filesystem network clock environment runner signer installer deployer executor custody registry or remote host exists in the adapter
  + caller-supplied public trust context remains evidence for core replay and is not promoted into platform trust

& [Rollback]
  + remove the cantor_compiler_mcp crate workspace member and Slice8 completion records
  + retain Slice7 core protocol and CLI plus all preserved Slice8 source SJS canonical justification plan matrix and phase lock records
